-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1116. two-traces.l4 reading the ledger through a rule WITH an
-- input: `closed to` of fn-lib.l4, whose body names `taken now` of taken.l4,
-- is called from both traces. It is a function and not a constant, but the
-- `taken now` in its body must read each trace's own ledger all the same. The
-- first trace gives two COMMITs and WITHIN 10, the second one COMMIT and
-- WITHIN 9, as each does alone.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fn-lib`

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    buy

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`shop` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY buy PROVIDED NOT `closed to` 1
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS TRUE HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `closed to` 1 ELSE TRUE) HENCE `shop`
    LEST FULFILLED

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go peek AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2

#TRACE `start` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Bob DOES go skip AT 1
    PARTY Bob DOES buy AT 2
